    "product": {
      "id": 897016,
      "name": "Shiro plums",
      "description": "Shiro plums are large, round, yellow plums with a mild, sweet flavor and a slightly tart skin. Their flesh is juicy, translucent, and has a tender, melting texture. Shiro plums are great for fresh eating, cooking, canning, and dessert. Some say that Shiro plum jam has a flavor similar to pear butter, with notes of candied lemon and soft floral sweetness. Shiro plum is a popular, heirloom Japanese plum introduced in 1899 by Luther Burbank. Famous for its translucent, golden-yellow skin and incredibly sweet, juicy flesh. It is prized for fresh eating, baking, and canning. I also dry them for a sweet/tart treat in my mixed dried fruit bags.",
